From 81e73434a2453171b311f5fbfb5930bed728a8bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:39:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Beginner clue scrolls

Beginner Treasure Trails: Read opens trail_cluetext (or the beginner map
interface) with the step, 34 steps in the server-only dbtable
trail_beginner_steps (anagram and cryptic npc talks, emote steps with Uri, map
digs, Charlie the Tramp's item tasks and Reldo's hot-cold strange device with
its temperature readings), Check steps, and the reward casket rolled from the
OSRS Wiki table (dbtable trail_beginner_casket) into trail_rewardinv with the
completion count message. Beginner STASH units: Build (Construction 12, planks,
nails, hammer, saw) sets the hh_constructed varbits, Search stores or takes
back the emote items. Scroll box (beginner) Open, and ::clue [step] [steps left].

NpcOpOverrides lets content take an npc op ahead of that npc's own handler for
the players it claims, so a clue step can take Talk-to on npcs that already
have dialogue (Cook, Hans, Doric, ...).
